From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:17:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/25] Skip a new Private texture's first page-up, behind a
 switch

Safari's compositor makes about ten 2368x256 Private render targets per
present, and each one builds a view of 148 guest-page runs, imports it
and blits it, on the exec's serial path, only to overwrite a texture
that already reads zero. REIMS_VGPU_PRIVATE_SKIP_PAGE_UP=1|2 skips that
first page-up: no view, no import, no paging buffer. Off by default.

Mapping reuse found nothing to reuse, because the guest puts other
physical pages behind the recycled ranges. So mapstat gains the stale
runs, the skips, the refusals and the mmaps with their time, and the
trun event gives each walk's run count and hash.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
